.Sh CAVEATS
Every buffer given to a constructor, and
.Fa data Ns .mem
and
.Fa dst Ns .mem ,
must not be
.Dv nullptr ,
and an fs reader's or fs writer's buffer must not be empty; this is assumed,
not checked.
.Pp
On a pipe, a terminal or a socket,
.Fn xft_reader_stream
and
.Fn xft_reader_read_all
on an fs or tcp reader keep reading until
.Fa limit
or
.Fa dst
is reached or the input ends, so they block until then.
.Pp
After an fs writer fails, the staged bytes are kept even if some were
already written, so flushing again can write them twice.
.Pp
Every read from a growable reader moves the remaining bytes, so its cost
grows with the bytes left.
.Pp
The growable writer's
.Fa drain_fd
on a regular file reads at most the size reported when it starts, so bytes
appended to the file after that are left for the next call.
.Pp
The tcp writer's
.Fa drain_fd
tries
.Xr sendfile 2
first on every call, so draining a socket or a pipe into it costs one
failed system call before the copy starts.
.Pp
Do not pass the zeroed result of a failed
.Fn xft_map_file_into_memory
to
.Fn xft_unmap_file_from_memory .
